From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 04:05:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: add clk_limit to name the clock that wedges
 msm8998

The stop_at bisect placed the msm8998 fabric wedge inside
core_power(POWER_ON): stop_at=5 leaves it unrun and the phone survives with
venus_core loaded, stop_at=6 runs it and netconsole -- verified end to end on
usb0 seconds earlier -- carries the marker and then nothing at all, with the
phone returning on the hardware watchdog.

On this SoC that call is one thing. vcodec_domains_enable() returns 0
immediately because msm8998_res declares no vcodec_pmdomains, and the
clk_set_rate() in core_clks_enable() is gated to V6 and V4-lite. The device's
own VIDEO_TOP_GDSC is already powered by then -- genpd brings it up during the
pm_runtime_get_sync() that reaches venus_runtime_resume(), and that is exactly
the path stop_at=5 survives. The interconnect votes have also already been
placed, for the same reason.

What is left is clk_prepare_enable() on "core", "iface", "bus" and "mbus". So
enable a prefix of them: clk_limit=N takes the first N, and the largest N that
still boots names the clock whose CBCR touch never returns.

Default -1 enables all of them, so this is inert unless asked for.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/pm_helpers.c | 21 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/pm_helpers.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/pm_helpers.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/pm_helpers.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/pm_helpers.c
@@ -38,6 +38,23 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Bring-up bisect, second stage. stop_at proved the msm8998 wedge is inside
+ * core_power(POWER_ON), and on this SoC that call reduces to this function:
+ * vcodec_domains_enable() returns immediately because msm8998_res declares no
+ * vcodec_pmdomains, and the clk_set_rate() above is V6/V4-lite only. The
+ * device's own VIDEO_TOP_GDSC is already on by then -- genpd powers it during
+ * the pm_runtime_get_sync() that got us here, which survives.
+ *
+ * So the bus dies on clk_prepare_enable() of one of "core", "iface", "bus",
+ * "mbus". clk_limit=N enables only the first N of them, and the largest N that
+ * still boots names the clock.
+ */
+static int clk_limit = -1;
+module_param(clk_limit, int, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(clk_limit,
+	"venus bring-up bisect: enable only the first N core clocks (-1 = all)");
+
 static int core_clks_enable(struct venus_core *core)
 {
 	const struct freq_tbl *freq_tbl = core->res->freq_tbl;
@@ -59,6 +76,9 @@
 	}
 
 	for (i = 0; i < res->clks_num; i++) {
+		if (clk_limit >= 0 && i >= clk_limit)
+			break;
+
 		if (IS_V6(core) || (IS_V4(core) && is_lite(core))) {
 			ret = clk_set_rate(core->clks[i], freq);
 			if (ret)
